From dec3c14243362bfbb9b8fe1504654999e76c4e3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "@dev/6" <dev-6@main.hh.invalid>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 23:06:33 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(agent-acp): back off respawning a host server that dies
 before initialize, for records that keep sessions (#37753)

hh/integration already keeps a record whose host listing failed out of later
reads (failedOnHost, 305fc1e0c), but only while the record keeps no session.
A record that keeps sessions is listed with its machines, rethrows, and is
spawned again at every pass: ahpd-codex-trial (0.15.0-rc.4, which carries
305fc1e0c) spawned node and logged "exited with code 9" at every pass for
dev-8 and dev-luna3, whose --env-file is gone.

For that case, per @cto (32654479): a host server that dies before the
handshake is remembered against what the record spawns (command, args, cwd,
env). A read before the next attempt time is answered with the same death and
spawns nothing; the wait doubles from 1 min, capped at 15 min; each real
attempt logs one line, "<provider>: server ended before initialize (<death>);
next spawn attempt in <n> min". A changed input or a listing that answers
clears it. A failure after the handshake keeps today's retry, and the
no-session path (failedOnHost) is unchanged.

Tests: a kept-session record with a gone env file logs one line over three
passes; a died-early server spawns once inside the window, again after it
with the wait doubled, at once on changed args, and an answering listing
resets the wait to 1 min. Red on hh/integration's catalog (2 failing).
agent-acp-failure 40/40; agent-acp 428/431, the 3 custody failures are the
same without this change (@ahpd/sdk not resolvable in this worktree's
install); tsc unchanged (19 pre-existing errors in untouched files).

Refs: #37753

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
