From 64ddcd26b88d4ded104bab3138ebce928941da66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "@dev/6" <dev-6@main.hh.invalid>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 23:11:01 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(agent-acp): one host-listing retry policy: failedOnHost
 becomes the same bounded backoff (#37753)

Per @cto (0de9edd2): two policies for "the host's listing server failed" in
one file is a second implementation, and failedOnHost's permanent stop is
the silent-outage shape (a transient failure left a no-session record on
stale watched rows until something recreated its object).

hostRetry replaces both failedOnHost and the kept-session map: keyed by
spawn inputs, the wait doubles from 1 min to 15 min, one line per spawn
("<provider>: server ended before initialize (...)" or "session/list
failed: ..."; "; next spawn attempt in <n> min"), cleared by a changed input
or a listing that answers. Two triggers: a record with no kept session
waits after any failure and answers from the watched rows meanwhile, as
before; a record that keeps sessions waits only after a pre-handshake death
and is answered with that failure meanwhile.

Tests: the missing-command no-session record now tries again after the wait
(the wait doubling to 2 min) instead of never; the machines fallback test
reads the new line; the kept-session pair is unchanged. Red on
hh/integration's catalog (3 failing). agent-acp 428/431: the 3 custody
failures are the same without this change (@ahpd/sdk unresolved in this
worktree's install); tsc unchanged.

Refs: #37753

